    "created_at": "2023-06-18T14:36:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-06-18T14:36:07Z",
    "body": "> @mfreed7 to be clear, not all my comments were nits. I don't understand the normative text.\r\n\r\nSorry, I didn’t mean nits, I meant comments. There were two comments about the structure of the nested if blocks. One is how to interpret them, and I think the intention is that a nested dt is ANDed with its parent dt. The other is the weird thing about a bdi element that is also an input element, and I agree with that question. I was assuming you and fantasai would help get that sorted out. Was the intention of the bdi clause to be “if the element is *nested inside* a bdi element”, or something?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
