    "created_at": "2023-06-19T03:30:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-06-19T03:31:15Z",
    "body": "@mfreed7\r\n\r\n> Was the intention of the bdi clause to be “if the element is nested inside a bdi element”, or something?\r\n\r\nNo, the intention is that `<bdi>` be treated the same as `<span dir=auto>` (which is, essentially, what it's defined as). The fact that there's a second, clearly false, check against the tag name if you take this conditional branch is a side-effect of grouping these two cases together.\r\n\r\nAn alternative would be possible to pull the `input/textarea dir=auto` cases out into a short-circuit case above the general `dir=auto/bdi` case... but there are some downsides to that approach:\r\n* It creates a more complicated set of conditionals for the forms case (since it now has to inline the higher-level dir=auto test).\r\n* It makes the switch cases order-dependent. (Imho, it's simpler to reason through when they aren't.)\r\n* It also breaks having top-level switch be, functionally speaking, a simple switch on the state of the `dir` attribute. I think this is a really nice effect (and afaict the core thesis) of bkardell's restructuring, and it's worth keeping...\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1596439798/reactions",
