    "updated_at": "2023-06-19T10:04:16Z",
    "body": "> It also breaks having top-level switch be, functionally speaking, a simple switch on the state of the dir attribute.\r\n\r\nDoesn't the `bdi` element break this? I agree that might be nice, but this PR doesn't reflect that. If we wanted to do that we should also define the missing state as we do for other attributes.\r\n\r\nI noticed a few other things:\r\n\r\n- \"is slotted\" I guess this means \"is assigned\"? It needs to be cross-referenced.\r\n- \"slotted elements\" is not defined. This should reference \"find slottables\" presumably? That would also remove the need for the note.",
