    "updated_at": "2023-06-21T13:23:43Z",
    "body": "> We don't gain as much now\r\n\r\n@annevk We gain a lot in making this section of the spec understandable, imho. I think bkardell's restructuring is a lot easier to follow than the original version, and better represents the underlying concepts.\r\n\r\n> all the changes make this hard to review\r\n\r\nMaybe it could have been done in two commits, one restructuring and one adding the new stuff; but the complexity of adding this shadow DOM stuff is what precipitated the restructuring, so it makes sense to have it all in one PR...\r\n\r\n> But only the strict interpretation would allow for ... the dt elements would only have to list the state\r\n\r\nThis seems very minor? I'd rather have the editorial structure map to the conceptual structure than drop a few words from the DTs, personally.",
